WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.200 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  located in the town of Pathan in India  is a 90 foot deep step well with an even  deeper connection to the past built  inside an opening in the ground  approximately 200 feet long and 65 feet  wide the step well is designed as a 7  level inverted temple throughout history  most monuments have been constructed by  men with the intention of honoring their  wives however Rani Kaval is different as  it was initially built as a memorial to  the king in the 11th century AD by his  wife hence it became known as the Queen  step while in the past deep wells were  common throughout India these walls were  primarily used to collect water however  they also became a place of socialising  and an important aspect of the community  - people of the time it features more  than 500 principal sculptures and at  least 1,000 smaller sculptures all in  religious or mythological imagery at the  trends peak there were roughly 3000  stepwells in India however today only  around a thousand remain Veronica Valle  serves as a valuable visual history to  teach and remind visitors about the  traditions of the past  [Music]

